{#- Once-per-suite mock-request-count helper (alef issue #443).

   Context variables (see src/e2e/codegen/mock_assertions/helper.rs for the full contract):
   - helper_name: method name
   - total_path: mock server's total-count endpoint path
   - one_path: mock server's single-key endpoint path

   Emits ONE private static method using `System.Net.Http.HttpClient` -- already in every
   generated test file's unconditional using-list (`test_file.rs`'s `using_imports` adds
   `using System.Net.Http;` and `using System.Threading.Tasks;` for every fixture, not gated on
   this helper), so this template adds no new `using` to gate on, matching this backend's Java
   counterpart's own reasoning. Callers build `pathAndQuery` from "{{ total_path }}?prefix=<p>"
   (mock.requests.total) or "{{ one_path }}?key=<k>" (mock.requests["<k>"]) -- see
   mock_assertions::model::MockQuery. Synchronous (`GetAwaiter().GetResult()`) rather than
   `async`/`await`, since call sites embed it directly inside a synchronous `Assert.*` expression
   -- xUnit test methods run outside any `SynchronizationContext`, so this cannot deadlock the
   way the same pattern would on ASP.NET or a WPF/WinForms UI thread. ~keep
#}

    private static int {{ helper_name }}(string baseUrl, string pathAndQuery)
    {
        using var client = new HttpClient();
        var body = client.GetStringAsync(baseUrl + pathAndQuery).GetAwaiter().GetResult().Trim();
        if (!int.TryParse(body, out var count))
        {
            throw new InvalidOperationException($"{{ helper_name }}: non-integer response body: {body}");
        }
        return count;
    }
